>>> Dynamic <<<
It is a method where routers automatically learn and update routes between networks using routing protocols.

1) RIP ( routing information protocol)
* It is a Distance Vector Routing Protocol that uses hop count as a metric to determine the best path.
* RIP allows routers to exchnage the routing information and automatically choose the shortest route based on the number of hops.

-> Hop count:
Hop count means the number of routers a packet travels/crosses to reach the destination.
example- 
* Router A --> Router B --> Router C
* Hop count = 2

-> RIP versions:
* RIP v1
It is an classfull routing protocol.
It does not support VLSM/CIDR.
Uses broadcast updates.
* RIP v2
Classeless routing protocol.
Supports VLSM/CIDR.
Uses multicast address 224.0.0.9

-> Basic CISCO RIP configurations:

Router(config) # router rip
Router(config-router) # version 2
Router(config-router) # network 192.168.10.0
Router(config-router) # exit

